[size=6][color=#00ccff][b]AbsoluteHOTAS 5.0.1[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]Direct HOTAS/HOSAS flight control, native ship actions, throttle detents, profiles, layers, and live tuning for Starfield.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

AbsoluteHOTAS reads DirectInput hardware natively and drives Starfield ship controls without vJoy or Joystick Gremlin. Version 5.0.1 is the current stable standalone release and the HOTAS module shipped in Absolute Suite 0.2.0-beta.1.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Core features[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Six-axis flight control:[/color][/b] pitch, yaw, roll, lateral strafe, vertical strafe, and absolute or rate-based throttle.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Native ship actions:[/color][/b] seventeen named ship functions, weapons, boost, strafe, targeting, power navigation, POV camera controls, and context-aware Select/Back inputs.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Live axis tuning:[/color][/b] responsive graphs for deadzones, saturation, inversion, response, calibration, and physical input position.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Throttle setup:[/color][/b] direct detent-zone tuning for zero thrust, maximum thrust, reverse behavior, boost, and set-by-feel adjustment.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Profiles and shift layers:[/color][/b] reusable base profiles, modifier-controlled layers, macros, and device-specific calibration.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Button output methods:[/color][/b] native function calls, Starfield key output, and HOTAS-owned custom actions where supported.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Automatic pilot context:[/color][/b] flight output parks when leaving the pilot seat and remains suspended through menus/loading.[/*]
[*][b]Fail-closed native gates:[/b] a runtime mismatch disables the affected operation instead of guessing or emitting unsafe fallback input.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Configuration menus[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Recommended:[/b] install Absolute Control, open the Pause Menu, select [color=#ffaa00][b]MOD OPTIONS[/b][/color], and choose [b]AbsoluteHOTAS[/b]. The native shared menu includes axes, buttons, throttle tuning, profiles, shift layers, macros, devices, and diagnostics.

AbsoluteHOTAS remains fully standalone. Without Absolute Control, open the retained Dear ImGui workbench from the main or pause menu with [font=Courier New]Ctrl+Alt+B[/font]. Existing INI, profile, and hotkey workflows remain available.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffaa00][b]Modular ownership warnings[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]AbsoluteZero:[/b] when installed with AbsoluteHOTAS, AbsoluteZero owns mouse pitch/yaw steering and HOTAS yields its pitch/yaw stick bindings. HOTAS continues to control roll, strafe, throttle, buttons, and profiles while retaining the shared writer hook. Install both only when you want mouse steering—not a joystick—to own pitch and yaw.

[b]Absolute Head Tracking:[/b] when installed, the standalone Head Tracking module owns cockpit camera composition and HOTAS parks its embedded legacy tracker. Flight controls and the Absolute Input Bus continue normally.

[b]Absolute Power:[/b] remains authoritative for power presets and activation. HOTAS supplies the optional Input Bus used for controller/POV preset capture.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Requirements and installation[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.242 or 1.16.244[/*]
[*][url=https://sfse.silverlock.org/]SFSE[/url] 0.2.20 or later[/*]
[*]No Starfield Address Library required[/*]
[*]OpenTrack with FreeTrack 2.0 output only when using the embedded fallback camera tracker[/*]
[/list]

Install normally with MO2 or Vortex, or place [font=Courier New]AbsoluteHOTAS.dll[/font] and [font=Courier New]AbsoluteHOTAS.ini[/font] in [font=Courier New]Data\SFSE\Plugins\[/font].

[b]User data is separate:[/b] updates must not overwrite [font=Courier New]AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini[/font] or the [font=Courier New]Profiles[/font] directory. Back up both before updating. A 4.0.x setup can update by replacing only the DLL and shipped default INI.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Known boundaries and reporting[/b][/color][/size][/center]

Renderer compatibility with third-party overlays, capture tools, frame-generation layers, and Proton graphics stacks is best effort for the legacy workbench. The Absolute Control menu does not use HOTAS's renderer hook. Set [font=Courier New][UI] bEnableWorkbench=false[/font] in the custom INI to install no HOTAS D3D12/DXGI hooks while retaining flight controls.

Please report reproducible crashes, configuration loss, stuck outputs, core-flight regressions, failed ship actions, hardware-specific mapping problems, or menu issues. Include the AbsoluteHOTAS version, Starfield/SFSE versions, device names, active profile/layer, reproduction steps, and a sanitized log with logging enabled.

